 "correction_note": "k04 F6 (correction proposed by XR31): F6's Z_eff = Z + (2 - K_B) beta^2 (s Delta - j)/(8 pi) is the flux's secant stiffness Pi/q; it is >= Z for every kernel convex in Y (F = s Delta - j = Y J_Y - J >= 0) and cannot fail, so it does not test stability.  The test is the slaved scalar's longitudinal coefficient C_L,eff = dg_N/dg_phi at fixed Pi.  On k04's own kernel and couplings (F3's Z = 8 beta^2) the slaved force g_phi = a0_loc Delta(g_N/a0_loc) peaks at g_N = 2.385 a0 (K_B = 0; 2.403 at K_B = 0.25; 2.323 with kappa tied on the alt footing) and falls linearly to zero at 155.2 a0 (177.4; 106.3), so C_L,eff < 0 on the whole band (-238.6 at 20 a0): the static scalar equation is not elliptic there and longitudinal perturbations grow at a rate ~ k (omega^2 = -0.86 (ck)^2 in the chain root's quadratic form at lambda = 1).  The band holds 17% / 15% of SPARC points (Upsilon 0.7, can / alt), a shell from 639 to 5154 AU around every solar-mass star, and wide binaries at 2-5 kAU.  'stable (F6)' should read 'UNSTABLE for 2.39 < g_N/a0 < 155: the four-form's feedback tilts the saturated kernel's flat branch downward'.  F1-F2 are unaffected; F3's RAR shift stands below 2.39 a0; F4's planets sit in the switched-off core (the '205 AU' should read ~639 AU); F5's 2 kAU number is computed on an unstable solution.",
